    "case_id": "509",
    "case_summary": "A 42-year-old man presented with fever, chills, and left flank discomfort. Medical history includes:- Recurrent urinary tract infections due to neurogenic bladder- Previous right nephrectomy for nonfunctioning pelvic kidney- Chronic hypomagnesemia requiring parenteral magnesium sulfate through a mediport twice weekly- Receives treatment both at home and at local infusion center\n\nInitial examination revealed:- Afebrile- No other significant physical examination findings noted in the report\n\nLaboratory Tests:- Serum lactate: 1.0 mmol/L (range: 0.4–2.0 mmol/L)- Serum magnesium: 0.66 mmol/L (range: 0.74–0.99 mmol/L)- Leukocytosis: 11,240 cells × 10⁶/L- Urinalysis: normalImaging Studies:- Chest radiograph: normalMicrobiology:- Initial blood cultures: positive for Gram-positive rods- Follow-up peripheral blood cultures: negative after five days- Mediport cultures: positive for Gram-positive rods after three days- 16S rRNA bacterial gene sequencing performed at CDC",
